# ENLENS claims

Prototype of the claim-centred redesign of the ENLENS pipeline. It extracts evidence-backed SDG impact claims from
source documents, checks the green hydrogen Value Chain Assessment (Peyerl & van der Zwaan 2024) against its cited
sources, and reports effects, synergies and trade-offs by segment, place, time and condition.

Check single claims in the browser:

```bash
pip install -e '.[gui]'
enlens-gui
```

Run the whole pipeline from the command line:

```bash
pip install -e '.[dev]'
pytest
enlens --ws pilot init
enlens --ws pilot load-vca 43621_2024_374_MOESM1_ESM.xlsx
enlens --ws pilot ingest sources/
```

The usage manual is in [docs/MANUAL.md](docs/MANUAL.md). The green hydrogen pilot (workspace, report and run notes)
is in `pilot/`; start with `pilot/RUN_NOTES.md` and `pilot/report/report.html`.

`tools/pdf_to_text.py` converts a folder of PDFs to page-preserving text files for upload (needs only `pypdf`).

Layout:

| Module | Role |
| --- | --- |
| `ingest.py` | PDF, HTML and text to documents and passages with page and character offsets |
| `vca.py` | VCA workbook (cell colours) to gold labels and cited references |
| `sources.py` | Match documents to references by DOI or wording |
| `retrieve.py` | BM25 ranking and the passage screen |
| `schema.py`, `prompts.py` | Output schemas and versioned prompts for split, extract, verify_set and verify |
| `tasks.py` | Create, export, run and validate model tasks (quote check, retries, dry-run checks, audits) |
| `llm.py` | Claude API, Ollama, other OpenAI-compatible servers, and an offline keyword baseline |
| `analysis.py` | Effects, candidate interactions, VCA support, label recovery, VCA consistency, audit agreement |
| `review.py` | Reviewer queue as CSV, decisions back as labels, gold-set export |
| `report.py` | `report.html` and CSV/JSON exports |
| `claimcheck.py` | Check one typed claim: search terms, passage ranking, grading, results and history |
| `benchmark.py` | Score a model against answers a reference model already gave |
| `gui/` | The claim checker: `app.py` (Streamlit pages), `core.py` (settings, projects, key, backends), `launch.py` |
